# Two Royal Treatments on one Ornithopter: the second Royal Role is the same player's second Role on that creature, so
# the state-based action puts the older one into the graveyard, where the token ceases to exist (CR 704.5z, 303.7a,
# 704.5d). The Ornithopter is a 1/3, not a 2/4. The second Royal Treatment targets a creature with ward that its own
# controller controls, so ward does not trigger (CR 702.21a: "an opponent controls") and Bot1, with no mana left,
# is asked for nothing: the spell resolves, which the Role that left the battlefield shows.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Royal Treatment
Royal Treatment
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Royal Treatment.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Royal Treatment.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald; Ornithopter; Royal
Bot1.Battlefield.Royal.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Royal Treatment; Royal Treatment
LeftBattlefield = Royal
